3.6. Results and discussion
3.6.1. Performance In terms of task completion rate, older participants completed 77.9% of the tasks and younger participants completed 100% of the tasks. For the older participants, the relatively difficult touch gestures were “Zoom,” “Draw,” and “Handwrite,” with 57.1%, 64.3%, and 67.9% successful tasks. In terms of task completion time, since the task completion time of the failed tasks was invalid (about 5.5%), these data were deleted before the covariance analysis was conducted. After deleting the invalid data, the older participants spent an average of 36.8 s per task (SD = 2.2) and the younger participants spent 18.5 s per task (SD = 1.2).
The correlation analysis, ANCOVA, and paired t-test were used to analyze the performance. First, all eight covariates were included in the ANCOVA model. Then, the covariates with a regression slope equal to 0 and those without signifi­ cant influence in the ANCOVA were removed; the remaining covariates will be reported separately. Since Mauchly’s test of sphericity in the ANOVA models was violated, a Huynh-Feldt correction was used. Furthermore, if the effects of the inde­ pendent variables were significant, the paired sample t-test method would be used to further analyze the impact of different levels on the dependent variable.
